  "body": "Keep large CAM projects inside local and cloud model context windows.\n\n## Scope\n- Add compact read options in `crates/app/src/mcp/`:\n  - Add a `summary` flag to `get_job` that omits full `machine.definition` blocks and unchanged operation defaults.\n  - Add a kind or category filter to `list_operation_types`.\n  - Add compact output options and a smaller chat default `limit` to `list_features` (currently defaults to `500` in `crates/app/src/mcp/features.rs`).\n- Add a core CAM tool subset preset (~20 to 25 common workflow tools) alongside the full 70-tool mode for small local models.\n- Enforce runtime limits in the chat worker loop:\n  - Cap characters per tool reply and append a truncation hint.\n  - Cap attached viewport images per turn.\n  - Cap tool-call rounds per turn.\n  - Prune old conversation turns while keeping the latest `get_job` summary.\n\nDone means: Compact MCP replies fit target budget limits in unit tests, and the chat loop enforces character truncation, image limits, round caps, and rolling history pruning without network calls.\n\nPart of #1773\n",
